<article class="env-definition" id="032F">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/032F">Definition <span data-tag="032F">10.161.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a domain with field of fractions $K$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $R$ is <em>N-1</em> if the integral closure of $R$ in $K$ is a finite $R$-module. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $R$ is <em>N-2</em> or <em>Japanese</em> if for any finite extension $L/K$ of fields the integral closure of $R$ in $L$ is finite over $R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>